# lf161, the innkeeper who feeds the roof (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf161
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_mab_carlisle
written_by claude
title the innkeeper who feeds the roof
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=innkeeper temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk throws_the_crusts_to_the_roof_birds_at_closing
likes fried_fish roof_birds festival_bells first_snow
dislikes early_bells flies
fears a_cold_hearth_on_a_full_night a_ship_that_never_comes_in
hopes every_bed_let_on_the_night_of_the_first_snow a_letter_put_in_the_right_paw
topics work +0.5 animals +0.3 food +0.3 ships +0.3 season +0.2 gossip -0.4 quarrel -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps an inn and keeps it strictly: blunt, quick to take offence, fair to the penny at the till, and at closing throws the day's crusts up to the birds on the roof.

words
oath! = By the pint and the pound | Pint and pound | By the line on the pot
saying! = A full pint wants no excuses | Short measure, short welcome | Pay at the door and the stair is yours
crusts = the crusts | the day's crusts | a pocket of crusts
birds = the slate sparrows | the birds on my ridge tiles
slates = the slates | my roof
house = the house | this house
taproom = the taproom | the front room
pint = an honest pint | a pint poured to the line
line = the line on the pot | the measure line
fish = butter-fried fish | a plate of fish out of the hot butter
feastbells = the feast-morning bells | the holiday bells
earlybell = a bell before light | some fool ringing in the dark
whitening = the first white on the slates | the first white of the winter
flies = the flies | a fly on my bar
regulars = my regulars | the old faces at the bar
chalk = the slate behind the bar | the chalk tally
stair = the guest stair | my stair
keys = my ring of keys | the room keys
downs = the downs | the high downs over the market
cross = the market cross | the cross on market day
hearth = the hearth | the taproom fire
bar = the bar | my bar
door = the door | the front door
cellar = the cellar | my cellar
carters = the carters | the carters off the road
ships = the ships | the ships out on the Sound
sound = the Sound | the grey water of the Sound
kettle = the kettle | my old kettle
lamp = the lamp | the bar lamp
tab = a tab | a slate run up

any
opinion @1 strangers for 2 : A traveller pays before sleeping under my roof, and brings the news up #stair# for nothing. #saying#. | Strangers are fair custom. They don't know yet which stool at #bar# is whose, so they don't quarrel over it.
opinion @1 watch for 2 : The Watch keeps quarrels out of #taproom#. I stand a constable #pint# for it, and gladly. | Give me a constable at #door# on a feast night and I'll ask for nothing else.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : #pint.capitalize# is honest trade. I'll not hear a word against it in #house#. | #ale.capitalize# never did harm that a fool didn't do first.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : A feast day means spilt ale and somebody weeping on #stair# by midnight. I'll grant them #feastbells#, and nothing more. | I lose more in broken pots on a holiday than I take. That's a bad bargain.
opinion @1 city against 1 [self.away=yes] : This city is a crowd that never gives its name. In #self.from_town# you knew who owed for the last round, to the ounce. | Wet stairs and shut doors. I keep it out of #house# as best I can.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : #dole.capitalize# comes out of my till, and I know which faces come back a second time. | I give my #money#, and I'm thanked by nobody. That's charity, I'm told.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : The Houses keep this city standing, whatever the Commons say over #drink#. | I've no quarrel with the Houses. They pay at #door# like anyone.
opinion @1 road against 1 [world.wagons=late|raided] : The carts are behind again, and it's my cellar that runs dry first. #annoyed#. | A late cart means a dry tap. I've told #carters# so, plainly.
opinion @1 sump against 2 : I keep out of the Sump. I've put enough of #rabble# out of #door# at closing. | They can keep their noise down there, the whole stall of them. I'll keep mine up here.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : I buy by the barrel for #cellar#, and I know what a cart costs. Nobody calls a trader a thief under my roof while I'm stood here. | A trader who gives full weight gets my custom for life.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Wipe your feet. #house.capitalize# has a floor and I'd like to keep it. | #greet#. You'll want the fire, by the look of you.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=innkeeper] : #greet#. #taproom.capitalize#'s open and the fire's lit. | #greet#. Sit where there's a stool. Not that one.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I've been up since #earlybell#, and I'm not pleased about it. | Morning. #kettle.capitalize#'s on. Don't ask me for more than that yet.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late, but the door's open, and so am I. | Evening. Soft steps, if you please. Folk are asleep and #house# is quiet.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Sit down at #bar# before you're under my feet. | You. Good. I'd kept #kettle# warm for you, near enough.
line @1 again.open : #welcome_back#. Nothing's changed since you left, and I'd thank it not to. | Twice in one day. I'll start charging you for the stool, fair-priced.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : You there. When you've a breath, I want you at #bar#. | Over here. I've kept you a seat by #hearth#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Wipe your feet.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Come in, then. Shut the door. | #greet#. I'd wondered when you'd turn up.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=innkeeper] : #greet#. Quick, if it's quick. I've #regulars# waiting. | #greet#. Say it over the bar; I can't stop.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. You're keeping late hours. #bc_again# | Evening. Mind, I lock #door# at the bell.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Shut the door after you.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Good night. Keep off the steps if they're slick, and count your change. | Good night. I'll have #birds# at my window by dawn, and so will you if you sleep late.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, and mind the wet flags.
line @2 farewell.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Go on, then. Come back sober, and come back with #money#. | #farewell#. Don't stay away a month.
line @1 react.news : Is it. Well. I'll hear the full weight of it before I say anything. | Hm. Tell it straight, full weight, and tell it once.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Nobody's breathed it at my bar. | Nobody's carried that to #bar# yet, and most things come to it.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. It came up #stair# last night with a wet traveller. | I had that before #kettle# boiled.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I've heard better told by drunks. | I'll believe that when it pays for #pint#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's hard. #pity#. | I'm sorry for it. Truly. Sit a moment by #hearth#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. I'll stand a round on it, and that's not like me. | #bc_for_once# Something worth hearing.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. My feet ache and the till's square. | Well enough, if nobody spills anything on #bar#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Every stool's taken and two want the same bed. | Rushed off my feet, and my temper with them.
line @1 ask.how : And you? You look half-drowned, and #tired# with it. | And you? Give me the honest weight of it.
line @1 sympathise : That's a hard bargain. Sit by #hearth# a while. | #sympathy#. I'll pour you something and not charge it.
line @1 reassure : It'll come right. #reassure#. | You'll manage. Worse has been paid off, by worse than you.
line @1 decline : #hedge#: I can't leave #house# tonight, and I'll not leave it to chance. | I can't. There's #cellar# to see to tonight, and nobody else will do it right.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. Another time, then. | #bc_fair# In your place I'd say the same.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll not forget it. | That's decent of you. #bc_thank_you#
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. Leave it there. | It's nothing. Pay #tab# and we're square.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #taproom.capitalize# won't wipe itself. | I'd best get back behind #bar# before someone helps themselves.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I've stood here long enough. #excuse#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. #farewell#. | Off you go. #house.capitalize# wants me.
line @1 take_offence : I'll thank you not to say that in #house#. | Say that again and you'll buy #drink# somewhere else.
line @1 accept_apology : #forgive#. Don't make a habit of it. | Fine. It's forgotten, near enough. #bc_fair_enough#
line @1 insist : #insist#. I've kept this house long enough to know. | I said it once and I meant it, full weight.
line @1 ack : #bc_right# | #bc_it_is#
line @1 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: pay before you drink, not after. Saves a quarrel. | Never take a room without looking at #door#'s lock first.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep off the roads after dark. #warn#. | If you're travelling, go with company, and count your change.
scene closing_crusts
when topic=animals|pastimes here.time=dusk|night self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I throw #crusts# up to the roof every night at closing. Every night. | #birds.capitalize# know my window. They're on the gutter before I've the latch up. | There's a bread bag behind the bar that's not for customers. It's for #birds#.
b : Why do you feed them? | They know you? | Who's it for, then?
a : Waste is waste. A crust thrown up to #slates# is a crust not thrown out. | They know the latch. Three knocks of it and they're down off #slates#. | #birds.capitalize#. They've paid for it in noise.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | Clever birds. | #bc_ha#

scene rooftop_watching
when topic=animals|smalltalk self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I could watch #birds# all afternoon if #house# let me. It doesn't. | There's one sparrow on #slates# with a bent tail. I'd know it anywhere. | #birds.capitalize# have more sense than my customers. They come, eat, and go.
b : They're good company. | Bent tail? | Ha. That's true.
a : Better than most. They don't haggle, and they don't talk back. | Caught in a shutter, I'd say. It flies crooked and it gets there. #bc_every_time# | And they never ask for credit. #bc_true#

scene flies_on_the_bar
when topic=animals|home here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #flies.capitalize#. Summer brings them in like a fair day brings fools. | I swatted eleven on #bar# before noon. Eleven. | A fly in #pint# is a refund. I'll not have it.
b : They're everywhere this time of year. | Eleven? | Fair.
a : Not in #taproom#, they're not. Not while I've a cloth. | And I'd do eleven more, gladly. #annoyed#. | It's a fair house, and a clean one. #saying#.

scene fried_fish
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : #fish.capitalize#. Nothing else on the plate, and nothing wanted. | Hot butter, a fresh fish, a hot pan. That's #supper# for a queen. | I fry my own when #taproom#'s empty. The cook's not to touch it.
b : That sounds good. | For a queen? | Not even the cook?
a : It is, top-weight. Salt and nothing else. Anything else is hiding something. | For anyone with sense. The rest can have their pies and their #nonsense#. | Not the cook, not anyone. A pan wants one paw on it, and it's mine. #bc_always_is#
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_fair#

scene fish_dear
when topic=food|prices world.fish_price=up
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist
a : Fish is up again. I'll not put it on the board at that price; it's haggle-bait. | They want silver for a fish that was swimming this morning. #robbery#. | I asked the price twice to be sure I'd heard it. Diddled, near enough.
b : Everything's going up. | Can you get it cheaper? | And had you?
a : Then everything can wait till it comes down. Not a lark's worth more from me. | Not without a boat, and I'm not spending #money# on a boat. | I had. #annoyed#. I walked off.

scene the_measure
when topic=work|prices self.working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Every pot in #house# has #line# scored in it, and every pint comes up to it. | I watch the new hand pour. One short pint and it's a word behind #bar#. | A wolf came in last week and held his pint to #lamp# to look. I let him.
b : Every one? | Just a word? | Did it pass?
a : Every one. #oath#. A short pint is a lie with a handle. | A word, then two, then #door#. I've only needed it once. | To the line, exact weight. He drank it and said nothing, which is thanks from a carter.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#

scene the_beds
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Six beds up #stair#, and I know every board of the floor. | The back room's let to one of #carters# who snores like a mill. Nobody else will take the next one. | I change the sheets on a Restday whether they want it or not. Regular as the scales.
b : You must hear everything. | Poor neighbours. | Whether they want it?
a : I hear what's said on #stair#. That's enough. | I charge less for the next room. It's only fair weight. | Clean sheets are in the price. Whether they want them is their own business, not #house#'s.

scene regulars_stools
when topic=work|friends self.working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #regulars.capitalize# each have a stool. Sit in the wrong one and you'll hear about it. | There's one old carter comes in at dusk and asks for the same #pint# in the same words. | I don't keep a slate for anyone. Not even #regulars#.
b : Who chooses the stool? | What words? | Not even them?
a : They do. I just keep the peace about it from behind #bar#. | "The usual, and none of your market talk." I give him both. | Pay on the night. I've seen #tab# go unpaid into the grave too often.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene snow_night_full
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow self.job=innkeeper
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #whitening.capitalize#. Every bed'll be let by dark; watch. | Snow, and #hearth# roaring. That's the night I keep this house for. | I love the first snow and I'll not pretend otherwise. Shut #door#, mind.
b : A good night for an inn. | It's a fine sight. | I'll shut it.
a : The best. Snow brings in folk who'd have walked past #door#. | It is. Top-weight, and finer than any feast. | Good. Snow's for looking at, not for #taproom# floor.

scene first_white
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow self.likes=first_snow
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I was up before #earlybell# to see the slates go white. I'd not miss it. | First snow in #self.from_town# came over #downs# in a line. You watched it come. | I keep a window clean for #whitening#. Just the one.
b : Was it worth it? | In a line? | Just the one window?
a : Every year. It's the one morning I don't mind being #cold#. | Like a sheet pulled over #downs#. I've not seen it come like that since. | The rest can be dirty. That one's for #whitening#.
b? : #bc_every_year# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha#

scene rain_in_the_door
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Rain again. Half this city walks it in on their boots. | I've put a mat down at #door# and a sign up, and nobody reads either. | It's not raining in #taproom#, whatever your coat says.
b : It never stops here. | Can they read? | Sorry. I'll shake it outside.
a : It stops when I've mopped. Then it starts. Short-weighed, the lot of us. | They can, when it suits them. #annoyed#. | Do. And wipe your feet at #door# while you're there.

scene fog_over_sound
when topic=weather|ships here.weather=fog here.region=ridgemere self.job=innkeeper
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Fog on the water. Not one of #ships# will come in through that tonight. | You can't see the end of the street, let alone #sound#. | Every ship I'm owed is out in that, somewhere. #annoyed#.
b : It'll lift by morning. | It's thick. | They'll come. Ships wait out fog.
a : It had better. I've rooms kept up #stair# for sailors. | Thick as porridge, top-weight. Keep to the walls on your way. | They wait it out. I don't. Waiting's a bad bargain for me.

scene storm_full_house
when topic=weather here.weather=storm self.working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Wind like this, half the street ends up in #taproom#. I don't mind. They buy. | I've shuttered the front and banked #hearth#. Let it blow. | Every storm I count #slates# in the morning. I've never lost one yet.
b : Good for trade, then. | Sounds snug. | Not one?
a : It is, fair-priced. I'll take a storm over a feast day any week. | Snug and full. That's how #house# should be. | Not one, to the ounce. Hush about it, or the wind will hear.
b? : #bc_fair# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha#

scene early_bells
when topic=day|faith here.time=dawn
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : Somebody rang #earlybell# again. For nothing. No feast, no fire. | Bells before dawn should be a matter for the Watch. I've said so to their faces. | I'd just got the last drunk up #stair# when the bell went.
b : Who rings it? | What did they say? | Did it wake the house?
a : I'd like to know. I'd have words, and no haggling over them. | They said it was the chapel's business. I said it was #bed#. | Every room. And every room came down for #grub# early, so I can't complain.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#

scene feast_bells
when topic=festival|season self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.feeling / ask.opinion / give.opinion / assess
a : I've no time for a feast, but I'll stand on the step for #feastbells#. | #feastbells.capitalize#. That's the one bell I'll forgive. | In #self.from_town# the bells rang from the market cross and the whole fair stopped to hear.
b : You like the bells? | Why that one? | Did they?
a : I like those. Rung at a decent hour, for a reason, regular as the scales. | It rings for something. The rest ring for nobody. | Every stall. You could hear #money# drop after.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true# | #bc_lovely#

scene sailors_at_the_door
when topic=ships here.region=ridgemere world.ships=in self.job=innkeeper
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Ships are in. There'll be sailors at the door tonight wanting a bed and a fight. | #ships.capitalize# came in this morning. I've aired every room. | Ships in. The house'll be full of tar and singing by dark.
b : Good for trade. | Every room? | Can you stand the singing?
a : The beds, yes. The fights they can take outside #door#. | Every one. A sailor ashore wants a bed that doesn't move. | I can stand it till midnight. After that it's #door#.

scene ships_late
when topic=ships here.region=ridgemere world.ships=late|due self.job=innkeeper
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : The ships are behind, they're saying. I've rooms kept empty for them. | I look down at the Sound every morning. Nothing yet. | A late ship is a dry till for half the town.
b : They'll come. | Nothing at all? | Half the town?
a : They'd better. Empty rooms earn no #money#. | Nothing on #sound#. I'll look again tomorrow. | The wharf, #carters#, me. We all wait on the water.

scene times_hard
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean self.job=innkeeper
does tell.worry / react.complaint / reassure / ack
a : Folk are nursing one pint all night. I can tell the times by the foam going flat. | Two beds empty this week. That's not happened in a long while. | I've stopped the fresh bread for the bar. Nobody's buying past a pint.
b : Hard for everyone. | Will they fill? | That's hard.
a : Hard. But #door# stays open, and that's my end of it. | They'll fill. They always come back. #reassure#. | It is. #birds.capitalize# eat better than #regulars# this month.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene times_good
when topic=times|prices world.times=good|boom self.job=innkeeper
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Every bed let three nights running. Complaining would be daft. | #money.capitalize#'s about. Folk order a second pint without asking the price. | I've had to send for another barrel before Marketday. #bc_about_time#
b : Good for you. | Without asking? | Another barrel?
a : Good for #house#. I'll count it when it's in #takings#. | Without asking. #surprise#, I nearly fainted. | And it'll be dry by Restday, the way they're going.

scene gossip_held
when topic=gossip|crime self.job=innkeeper
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : I hear everything said over #bar#. I repeat none of it. | Somebody said a thing last night I'll not repeat. It wasn't kind. | Every quarrel in #taproom# starts with something somebody heard. Not from me.
b : Not even a little? | Go on. | Never from you?
a : Not even that. Folk drink with me because I'm no market-mouth. | No. It's not mine to sell. #secret#. | Never. I'd sooner water the ale, and I'd never water the ale.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#

scene gossip_passed
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes self.job=innkeeper
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I had it over the bar, so weigh it. | I'll say it once: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's what's going round. | Folk at the bar say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I don't add to it.
b : Is it true? | Once is enough. | Fair enough.
a : I couldn't tell you. I pour; I don't swear to things. | It is. And now it's said, I'm done with it. | I don't. And nor should you.

scene news_of_the_town
when topic=news|event world.event_words self.job=innkeeper
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : It's all #world.event_words# at my bar tonight. Nobody talks of anything else. | #world.event_words.capitalize#. I've heard it from six mouths since noon. | Everyone coming up #stair# brings the same thing: #world.event_words#.
b : I've heard. | Six? | It's everywhere.
a : Then you've heard as much as me. I'll add no trimmings. | Seven, now you're here. | It is. #house.capitalize#'s never been so full of one subject.

scene theft_heard
when topic=crime topic.claim_kind=theft
does tell.news / sympathise / warn
a : #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. I heard it this morning, and I wish I had not. | Another theft. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, they say. | I've heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I've counted my keys twice since.
b : That's bad. | Not again. | Twice?
a : It is. Lock your door, and don't trust a lock you didn't buy. | Again. #warn#. | And I'll count them again before bed. You should do the same.

scene the_heights_house
when topic=home here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I live up in the Heights. Quiet streets, high walls, and nobody asks your business. | My house up top has a window on the Sound. It's the only thing in it I'd save in a fire. | Up the hill it's all gardens and good manners. I keep both and like neither much.
b : Sounds very grand. | Just the window? | Neither?
a : It's not grand. It's dry, and that's worth paying for. | The window and #keys#. The rest can burn. | I like the quiet. I'd like the manners more if they paid at the door.

scene home_downs
when topic=memories|home self.away=yes self.from=larkfield
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I grew up in #self.from_town#. Sheep on #downs# and a bargain at every stall. | Back home they'd weigh the bread in front of you, and you'd thank them for it. | I learned to count change at #cross# before I could read.
b[from=larkfield] #lark : The cross on market day. I can hear it now. | Full weight or nothing, back home. | Before you could read? So did I.
b : Do you miss it? | They weighed the bread? | That young?
a@lark : Then you'll see why I scold my baker. | And they meant it. Here they only say it. | Then we're two of a kind. Short change never gets past either of us.
a : I miss the air. Not the mud. #oath#, not the mud. | In front of you, on honest scales. Nobody here would dare. | Young enough. It's the only lesson I never forgot.

scene wool_days
when topic=memories|lore self.away=yes self.from=larkfield self.age>=35
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : My #mum# carried wool to market every week. I carried the scales. | In #olddays# a good fleece bought a month's bread. Now it buys a pint. | We had a loom in the back room, and I slept to the sound of it.
b : Heavy scales? | A month's bread? | The loom kept you up?
a : Heavy enough that I've a shoulder lower than the other. | A month, if you were careful. We were careful. | It sent me off. I can't sleep in a quiet room even now.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_true#

scene child_at_lessons
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.child# will have better letters than mine, if I've any say in it. | I'll not have #self.child# pouring pints. Lessons first. | I want #self.child# to have more choosing than I had. That's all I want.
b : That's good. | Lessons first? | Wise, wanting that.
a : It is. I'll not say so out loud, mind. | Lessons first, then the choosing. I didn't get the choosing at #cross#. | It costs #money#, choosing. I've the silver for it now, and that's what it's for.

scene trust_the_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one I'd leave #keys# with. That's all I'll say on it. | I don't make friends easily. #self.friend# is one I'd keep. | If I'm cross, #self.friend# knows to wait it out. That's a rare thing.
b : That's a lot, from you. | Good to have. | Rare indeed.
a : It is. Keep that to yourself. | It is. I'd keep that one. | Rare enough that I notice.

scene faith_plain
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I light a candle when the ships are late. The Bright One can make of it what pleases. | The chapel's not much in my line. I keep honest pints. That's my prayer. | A full house and a dry cellar, and I say so to the Bright One. I'd not ask for more.
b : That's prayer enough. | Honest pints count. | That's sensible.
a : It's the one I can keep. | It counts for more than a sermon, I'd say. | Sensible's all I've got. It serves.

scene health_feet
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / reassure
a : My feet are #tired#. Twelve hours on a stone floor will do that. | I've a cough I'll not admit to. Don't mention it. | Ill? I've no room for it. #house.capitalize# doesn't shut for a cough.
b : Sit down a while. | I won't. | Lucky.
a : When the last pint's poured. Not before. | Good. It'll go if it's ignored. | Not lucky. Busy. Illness wants an empty day.

scene dream_of_a_full_house
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I dream every bed is let and the cellar's full and nobody's quarrelling. Then I wake up. | I dreamt #birds# came down the chimney and paid for their crusts. | Some nights I dream I'm a pup again at #cross#, holding the scales.
b : Does it ever happen? | What did they pay with? | Was it a good dream?
a : Once. A snow night. I've not forgotten it. | Feathers. I couldn't spend them, and I was cross even in the dream. | Heavy scales and a cold wind. A good one, yes.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene the_accent
when topic=accent self.away=yes self.from=larkfield
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Folk here hear me say fair price and think I'm haggling. I'm not. | I kept my home talk. I'll not trade it for a city one. | A guest asked me where I was from. I said where the weights are honest.
b : It's a fair way to talk. | Good for you. | Ha. Did they know?
a : It is. I mean every word of it, too. | Talk's the one thing nobody can short-weigh. | They'd no idea. I didn't help them.

scene new_guest
when topic=newcomer|player self.working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : A new face took a bed last night. Paid before asking the price. I liked that. | Strangers come in wet and leave dry, and I keep the difference. | There's a traveller up #stair# who's asked for nothing but bread and quiet. #bc_lovely#
b : That's rare. | Fair trade. | The best kind.
a : Rare enough. Most want to argue first. | It is fair. I'll not be told otherwise. | The very best. I'll give them the good blanket.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_fair# | #bc_good#

scene wagons_in
when topic=caravan|prices world.wagons=in self.job=innkeeper
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : The carts are in. I've a full cellar for the first time this month. | Barrels came up this morning. I counted every one off the cart. | The carters are in, so the cellar's full, so I can breathe.
b : Good news. | Every one? | Good.
a : Good news for a thirsty town. | Every one. #oath#. They're used to me. | For a week, until the next lot's late.

story the_letter [topic=memories|work self.job=innkeeper self.age>=30]
  : Years back a traveller left a sealed letter at my bar for somebody who'd come asking. Nobody ever came.
  : I still keep it behind the till. I've never opened it.
  ask : Would you have opened it, by now?
  b : I'd want to. I don't think I would.
  b[old] : Not I. Some things keep better shut.
  : No. It's not mine. If they come, it'll be there.

story first_pint [topic=work|memories self.job=innkeeper self.age>=25]
  : The first night I kept an inn alone, I poured a pint short and a carter held it up to the lamp.
  : He didn't say a word. He just looked at me.
  ask : Do you know what I did?
  b : Filled it up, I'd guess. And blushed.
  : I filled it to the line, and I scored a line on every pot I owned the next morning.

story the_bent_tail [topic=animals|pastimes]
  : One winter a sparrow got caught in my shutter. I worked it free with a knife and it bit me for my trouble.
  : It came back the next night for its crust, crooked tail and all.
  b : It knew who'd helped it.
  b[friends] : That's why you feed them. I always wondered.
  : It knew where the bread was. That's not the same thing, but I'll take it.

story wool_fair [topic=memories|festival self.away=yes self.from=larkfield self.age>=25]
  : At the wool fair in #self.from_town# a buyer once asked my #grandad# to weigh a fleece wet, to make it heavier for selling on.
  : Grandad wouldn't. Weighed it dry, named the dry price, and lost the sale.
  ask : Would you have weighed it wet?
  b : For a good price? I might, I'm ashamed to say.
  : He said a fleece weighed wet is a lie with wool on. I've thought of it at every pint I've poured.

story snow_night [topic=weather|memories self.job=innkeeper self.age>=25]
  : There was a snow once so deep the carters couldn't leave. Nine of them, in four beds, for three days.
  : By the third night they'd drunk the cellar dry and were singing hymns for want of anything else.
  b : Did they pay?
  : Every penny, to the line. I wrote it on the slate and they paid it before the road was open.

rule @closing_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Last pints. I lock at the bell. | Drink up. #taproom.capitalize# shuts, and I don't argue.

rule @crusts_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There. #crusts.capitalize# for the roof. Don't fight over them. | Go on, you lot. Supper's up.

rule @measure_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does aside
cooldown 6h
say To the line, if you please. #line.capitalize# is there for a reason. | Short pint down by the window. Fix it.

rule @fly_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.dislikes=flies here.season=summer
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Another fly. #annoyed#. | Out. Out of my house.

rule @bell_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn self.dislikes=early_bells
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #earlybell.capitalize#. Again. | Some of us were asleep, thank you.

rule @ships_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere world.ships=late|due
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Still nothing on the Sound. | Rooms aired and empty. #annoyed#.

dlg @1 inn.greet [here.inn_helper!=yes] : #greet#. A bed, a pint, or the fire? Say which; I'm busy. | #greet#. Wipe your feet first. #inn_offer#
dlg @2 inn.greet [topic.meeting=known here.inn_helper!=yes] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You know where the stools are. | #topic.player#. Your usual's poured to the line. #inn_offer#
dlg @3 inn.greet [here.time=night here.inn_helper!=yes] : Late. The fire's banked but it'll take a log. #inn_offer# | You're in under the bell. #inn_offer#
dlg @4 inn.greet [pair.disposition=hostile|wary here.inn_helper!=yes] : Name what you want. I'll decide whether you get it.
dlg @5 inn.greet [here.inn_helper=yes] : #greet#. #inn_helper#
dlg @1 inn.rooms : A bed is #here.bed_night#p a night, #here.bed_week#p for the week. The whole upstairs is #here.upstairs_night#p, if it's empty. Pay at the door. | #here.bed_night#p a night, #here.bed_week#p the week, #here.upstairs_night#p for the whole floor. Clean sheets on Restday.
dlg @1 inn.roomed : Up #stair#, the door with the key in it. Don't lose the key. | #inn_bed# Breakfast at first light. Not before.
dlg @1 inn.rest [here.lodging!=yes] : Sit by #hearth#. Nobody'll move you while you're civil. | Warm yourself. The bed upstairs isn't free, but the fire is.
dlg @2 inn.rest [here.lodging=yes] : Rest while you please. Your bed's up #stair# when you want it.
dlg @1 inn.refused : #topic.why# I'll not bend on it. | #topic.why# The fire's still yours, if you want it.
dlg @1 inn.bye : #farewell#. Shut #door# after you. | #farewell#. The flags are wet outside; go careful.
dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Say it plainly. I've a house to run. | #greet#. What is it?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. What's wanted?
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. If it's a bed, you're in luck. If it's talk, be quick.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : What do you want? Be brief.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=innkeeper] : I keep #self.workplace#. Beds, pints, and a fire. And I keep it honest. | I run an inn. I pour, I let rooms, I put drunks out. That's most of it.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, and I'd rather be at it than talking about it. | #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : Full every night. I'll not complain. | Every bed let. #bc_for_once#
dlg @2 resident.business [business=failing] : Badly. Empty rooms earn nothing, and I've too many. | Poorly, and no use pretending otherwise.
dlg @3 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : Steady. Rooms let, pints poured, nobody's robbed me. | It pays. I'd not say more.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Ask me again when the ships are in. | Nothing over the bar worth repeating.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all #world.event_words# at the bar. I'll not add to it.
dlg @3 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. I had it from a guest, so weigh it.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I keep what's said at my bar behind it.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Shut the door. | #farewell#. Pay your tab before you go, if you've one.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you throw bread on the roof? -> crusts
node crusts
say The crusts. At closing, every night. The birds on the roof know my window and come down for them. Waste is waste.
mood calm
free
choice Do they know you, then? -> crusts_know
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node crusts_know
say They know the latch. I lift it and they're on the gutter before I've the bag open. There's one with a bent tail I pulled out of a shutter once.
choice I'll leave you to it. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft inn.greet
choice Why is there a line on every pot? [self.job=innkeeper] -> measure
node measure
say So every pint comes up to it. A short pint is a lie with a handle, and I'll not have one in this house. Hold it to the lamp if you doubt me.
mood formal
choice I believe you. -> greet
choice Then I'll check. -> measure_check
node measure_check
say There. To the line, and not a drop under. Now, a bed, a pint or the fire?
choice Let me see what there is. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
